msgstr "Date on which the agreement commences."

msgid "CommencementDate_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "Technical note: in IFC this property takes IfcDate as value."

msgid "TerminationDate"
msgstr "Termination Date"

msgid "TerminationDate_DEFINITION"
msgstr "Date on which the agreement terminates."

msgid "TerminationDate_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "Technical note: in IFC this property takes IfcDate as value."

msgid "Options"
msgstr "Options"

msgid "Options_DEFINITION"
msgstr "A statement of the options available in the agreement."

msgid "ConditionCommencement"
msgstr "Condition Commencement"

msgid "ConditionCommencement_DEFINITION"
msgstr "Condition of property provided on commencement of the agreement e.g. cold shell, warm lit shell, broom clean, turn-key."

msgid "Restrictions"
msgstr "Restrictions"

msgid "Restrictions_DEFINITION"
msgstr "[[Restrictions]] that may be placed by a competent authority."

msgid "ConditionTermination"
msgstr "Condition Termination"

msgid "ConditionTermination_DEFINITION"
msgstr "Condition of property required on termination of the agreement e.g. cold shell, warm lit shell, broom clean, turn-key."

msgid "IfcSpatialZone"
msgstr "Spatial Zone"

msgid "IfcSpatialZone_DEFINITION"
msgstr "A spatial zone is a non-hierarchical and potentially overlapping decomposition of the project under some functional consideration. A spatial zone might be used to represent a thermal zone, a construction zone, a lighting zone, a usable area zone. A spatial zone might have its independent placement and shape representation."

msgid "Width"
msgstr "Width"

msgid "Width_DEFINITION"
msgstr "The width of the object. Only given, if the object has constant thickness (prismatic)."

msgid "Height"
msgstr "Height"

msgid "Height_DEFINITION"
msgstr "Characteristic height."

msgid "IfcTransportationDevice"
msgstr "Transportation Device"

msgid "IfcTransportationDevice_DEFINITION"
msgstr "Abstract intermediate supertype for transportation devices."

msgid "CapacityPeople"
msgstr "Capacity People"

msgid "CapacityPeople_DEFINITION"
msgstr "[[Capacity]] of the transportation element measured in numbers of person."

msgid "CapacityPeople_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "Technical note: in IFC this property takes IfcCountMeasure as value."

msgid "CapacityWeight"
msgstr "Capacity Weight"

msgid "CapacityWeight_DEFINITION"
msgstr "[[Capacity]] of the transport element measured by weight."

msgid "CapacityWeight_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "Technical note: in IFC this property takes IfcMassMeasure as value."

msgid "IfcVirtualElement"
msgstr "Virtual Element"

msgid "IfcVirtualElement_DEFINITION"
msgstr "A virtual element is a special element used to provide imaginary, placeholder, or provisional areas, volumes, and boundaries. Virtual elements are usually not displayed and do not have quantities, associated materials, and other measures."

msgid "IfcZone"
msgstr "Zone"

msgid "IfcZone_DEFINITION"
msgstr "A zone is a group of spaces, partial spaces or other zones. These spaces may or may not be adjacent. A zone does not have its own shape representation. Zone structures may not be hierarchical (in contrary to the spatial structure of a project - see _IfcSpatialStructureElement_), i.e. one individual _IfcSpace_ may be associated with zero, one, or several _IfcZone_'s. _IfcSpace_'s are grouped into an _IfcZone_ by using the objectified relationship _IfcRelAssignsToGroup_ as specified at the supertype _IfcGroup_. For example, a zone might be used to represent an apartment as a group of spaces."

msgid "IfcAlignment"
msgstr "Alignment"

msgid "IfcAlignment_DEFINITION"
msgstr "For the purposes of IFC the English term 'alignment' defines three separate but closely interconnected concepts."

msgid "IfcBuildingStorey"
msgstr "Building Storey"

msgid "IfcBuildingStorey_DEFINITION"
msgstr "The building storey has an elevation and typically represents a (nearly) horizontal aggregation of spaces that are vertically bound."

msgid "EntranceLevel"
msgstr "Entrance Level"

msgid "EntranceLevel_DEFINITION"
msgstr "Indication whether this building storey is an entrance level to the building (TRUE), or (FALSE) if otherwise."

msgid "EntranceLevel_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "Technical note: in IFC this property takes IfcBoolean as value."

msgid "AboveGround"
msgstr "Aboveground"

msgid "AboveGround_DEFINITION"
msgstr "Indication whether this building storey is fully above ground (TRUE), or below ground (FALSE), or partially above and below ground ([[UNKNOWN]]) - as in sloped terrain."

msgid "AboveGround_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "Technical note: in IFC this property takes IfcLogical as value."

msgid "LoadBearingCapacity"
msgstr "Load Bearing Capacity"

msgid "LoadBearingCapacity_DEFINITION"
msgstr "Maximum load bearing capacity of the floor structure throughout the storey as designed."

msgid "LoadBearingCapacity_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "Technical note: in IFC this property takes IfcPlanarForceMeasure as value."

msgid "ElevationOfSSLRelative"
msgstr "Elevation of SSL Relative"

msgid "ElevationOfSSLRelative_DEFINITION"
msgstr "Elevation of the top surface of the structural slab level given in elevation above the local zero height. If the level varies and there is no significantly more prominent elevation, then this property may be omitted. In case of any inconsistency with the geometric positioning of the top surface, the geometric representation takes precedence."

msgid "ElevationOfSSLRelative_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "Technical note: in IFC this property takes IfcLengthMeasure as value."

msgid "ElevationOfFFLRelative"
msgstr "Elevation of FFL Relative"

msgid "ElevationOfFFLRelative_DEFINITION"
msgstr "Elevation of the top surface of the finished floor level given in elevation above the local zero height. If the level varies and there is no significantly more prominent elevation, then this property may be omitted. In case of any inconsistency with the geometric positioning of the top surface, the geometric representation takes precedence."

msgid "ElevationOfFFLRelative_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "Technical note: in IFC this property takes IfcLengthMeasure as value."

msgid "GrossHeight"
msgstr "Gross Height"

msgid "GrossHeight_DEFINITION"
msgstr "[[Standard]] gross height of this storey, from the top surface of the construction floor, to the top surface of the construction floor or roof above. Only provided is there is a constant height."

msgid "NetHeight"
msgstr "Net Height"

msgid "NetHeight_DEFINITION"
msgstr "[[Standard]] net height of this storey, from the top surface of the construction floor, to the bottom surface of the construction floor or roof above. Only provided is there is a constant height."

msgid "GrossPerimeter"
msgstr "Gross Perimeter"

msgid "GrossPerimeter_DEFINITION"
msgstr "Gross perimeter at the outer contour of the object."

msgid "GrossFloorArea"
msgstr "Gross Floor Area"

msgid "GrossFloorArea_DEFINITION"
msgstr "Sum of all gross floor areas within the spatial structure element."

msgid "NetFloorArea"
msgstr "Net Floor Area"

msgid "NetFloorArea_DEFINITION"
msgstr "Sum of all net usable floor areas."

msgid "IfcExternalSpatialElement"
msgstr "External Spatial Element"

msgid "IfcExternalSpatialElement_DEFINITION"
msgstr "The external spatial element defines external regions at the building site.; * logically - for example, an instance of _IfcExternalSpatialElement_ could represent the air space around the building without having an own shape representation, or; * physically - for example, an instance of _IfcExternalSpatialElement_ could represent the sloping ground around the building to identify the part of the external building envelop that is below ground."

msgid "IfcFacility"
msgstr "Facility"

msgid "IfcFacility_DEFINITION"
msgstr "A Facility (derived from _IfcSpatialStructureElement_) may be an _IfcBuilding_, an _IfcBridge_, an _IfcRailway_, an _IfcRoad_, an _IfcMarineFacility_ (or any other type of built facility defined in the future, such as IfcTunnel)."

msgid "IfcFacilityPart"
msgstr "Facility Part"

msgid "IfcFacilityPart_DEFINITION"
msgstr "_IfcFacilityPart_ provides for spatial breakdown of built facilities. It may be further specialised according to the type of facility being broken down."

msgid "Area"
msgstr "Area"

msgid "Area_DEFINITION"
msgstr "Calculated area for the object."

msgid "IfcFeatureElementAddition"
msgstr "Feature Element Addition"

msgid "IfcFeatureElementAddition_DEFINITION"
msgstr "A feature element addition is a specialization of the general feature element, that represents an existence dependent element which modifies the shape and appearance of the associated master element. The _IfcFeatureElementAddition_ offers the ability to handle shape modifiers as semantic objects within the IFC object model that add to the shape of the master element."

msgid "IfcFeatureElementSubtraction"
msgstr "Feature Element Subtraction"

msgid "IfcFeatureElementSubtraction_DEFINITION"
msgstr "The _IfcFeatureElementSubtraction_ is specialization of the general feature element, that represents an existence dependent element which modifies the shape and appearance of the associated master element. The _IfcFeatureElementSubtraction_ offers the ability to handle shape modifiers as semantic objects within the IFC object model that subtract from the shape of the master element."

msgid "IfcImpactProtectionDevice"
msgstr "Impact Protection Device"

msgid "IfcImpactProtectionDevice_DEFINITION"
msgstr "An impact protection device is a component used to protect other built elements from kinetic damage."

msgid "IfcSite"
msgstr "Site"

msgid "IfcSite_DEFINITION"
msgstr "A site is a defined area of land, possibly covered with water, on which the project construction is to be completed. A site may be used to erect, retrofit or turn down building(s), or for other construction related developments."

msgid "LandID"
msgstr "Land ID"

msgid "LandID_DEFINITION"
msgstr "Identification number assigned by the statutory registration authority to a land parcel."

msgid "LandID_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "Technical note: in IFC this property takes IfcIdentifier as value."

msgid "IsPermanentID"
msgstr "Is Permanent ID"

msgid "IsPermanentID_DEFINITION"
msgstr "Indicates whether the identity assigned to the object is permanent (= TRUE) or temporary (=FALSE)."

msgid "IsPermanentID_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "Technical note: in IFC this property takes IfcBoolean as value."

msgid "LandTitleID"
msgstr "Land Title ID"

msgid "LandTitleID_DEFINITION"
msgstr "Identification number assigned by the statutory registration authority to the title to a land parcel."

msgid "LandTitleID_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "Technical note: in IFC this property takes IfcIdentifier as value."

msgid "BuildableArea"
msgstr "Buildable Area"

msgid "BuildableArea_DEFINITION"
msgstr "The area of site utilization expressed as a maximum value according to local building codes."

msgid "BuildableArea_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "Technical note: in IFC this property takes IfcAreaMeasure as value."

msgid "SiteCoverageRatio"
msgstr "Site Coverage Ratio"

msgid "SiteCoverageRatio_DEFINITION"
msgstr "The ratio of the utilization, [[TotalArea]] / [[BuildableArea]], expressed as a maximum value. The ratio value may be used to derive [[BuildableArea]]."

msgid "SiteCoverageRatio_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "Technical note: in IFC this property takes IfcPositiveRatioMeasure as value."

msgid "FloorAreaRatio"
msgstr "Floor Area Ratio"

msgid "FloorAreaRatio_DEFINITION"
msgstr "The ratio of all floor areas to the buildable area as the maximum floor area utilization of the site as a maximum value according to local building codes."

msgid "FloorAreaRatio_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "Technical note: in IFC this property takes IfcPositiveRatioMeasure as value."

msgid "BuildingHeightLimit"
msgstr "Building Height Limit"

msgid "BuildingHeightLimit_DEFINITION"
msgstr "Allowed maximum height of buildings on this site - according to local building codes."

msgid "BuildingHeightLimit_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "Technical note: in IFC this property takes IfcPositiveLengthMeasure as value."

msgid "TotalArea"
msgstr "Total Area"

msgid "TotalArea_DEFINITION"
msgstr "Total planned area for the site. Used for programming the site space."

msgid "TotalArea_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "Technical note: in IFC this property takes IfcAreaMeasure as value."

msgid "GrossArea"
msgstr "Gross Area"

msgid "GrossArea_DEFINITION"
msgstr "Gross [[Area]] of the object. Openings, recesses, projections and cut-outs are not taken into account."

msgid "MaxAmbientTemp"
msgstr "Max Ambient Temp"

msgid "MaxAmbientTemp_DEFINITION"
msgstr "Maximum ambient temperature of the site used as a basis of design."

msgid "MaxAmbientTemp_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "Technical note: in IFC this property takes IfcThermodynamicTemperatureMeasure as value."

msgid "MinAmbientTemp"
msgstr "Min Ambient Temp"

msgid "MinAmbientTemp_DEFINITION"
msgstr "Minimum ambient temperature of the site used as a basis of design."

msgid "MinAmbientTemp_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "Technical note: in IFC this property takes IfcThermodynamicTemperatureMeasure as value."

msgid "IfcSpace"
msgstr "Space"

msgid "IfcSpace_DEFINITION"
msgstr "A space represents an area or volume bounded actually or theoretically. Spaces are areas or volumes that provide for certain functions within a building."

msgid "FinishCeilingHeight"
msgstr "Finish Ceiling Height"

msgid "FinishCeilingHeight_DEFINITION"
msgstr "[[Height]] of the suspended ceiling (from top of flooring to the bottom of the suspended ceiling). To be provided only if the space has a suspended ceiling with constant height."

msgid "FinishFloorHeight"
msgstr "Finish Floor Height"

msgid "FinishFloorHeight_DEFINITION"
msgstr "[[Height]] of the flooring (from base slab without flooring to the flooring height). To be provided only if the space has a constant flooring height."

msgid "NetPerimeter"
msgstr "Net Perimeter"

msgid "NetPerimeter_DEFINITION"
msgstr "Net perimeter at the floor level of this space. It excludes those parts of the perimeter that are created by by virtual boundaries and openings (like doors). It is the measurement used for skirting boards and may include the perimeter of internal fixed objects like columns."

msgid "GrossWallArea"
msgstr "Gross Wall Area"

msgid "GrossWallArea_DEFINITION"
msgstr "Sum of all wall (and other vertically bounding elements, like columns) areas bounded by the space. It includes the area covered by elements inside the wall area (doors, windows, other openings, etc.)."

msgid "NetWallArea"
msgstr "Net Wall Area"

msgid "NetWallArea_DEFINITION"
msgstr "Sum of all wall (and other vertically bounding elements, like columns) areas bounded by the space. It excludes the area covered by elements inside the wall area (doors, windows, other openings, etc.)."

msgid "GrossCeilingArea"
msgstr "Gross Ceiling Area"

msgid "GrossCeilingArea_DEFINITION"
msgstr "Sum of all ceiling areas of the space. It includes the area covered by elementsinside the space (columns, inner walls, etc.). The ceiling area is the real (and not the projected) area (e.g. in case of sloped ceilings)."

msgid "NetCeilingArea"
msgstr "Net Ceiling Area"

msgid "NetCeilingArea_DEFINITION"
msgstr "Sum of all ceiling areas of the space. It excludes the area covered by elementsinside the space (columns, inner walls, etc.). The ceiling area is the real (and not the projected) area (e.g. in case of sloped ceilings)."

msgid "IfcTransportElement"
msgstr "Transport Element"

msgid "IfcTransportElement_DEFINITION"
msgstr "A transport element is a generalization of all transport related objects that move people, animals or goods within a Facility. The _IfcTransportElement_ defines the occurrence of a transport element, that (if given), is expressed by the _IfcTransportElementType_."

msgid "IfcVehicle"
msgstr "Vehicle"

msgid "IfcVehicle_DEFINITION"
msgstr "Piece of equipment designed to transport people or cargo."

msgid "IfcVibrationDamper"
msgstr "Vibration Damper"

msgid "IfcVibrationDamper_DEFINITION"
msgstr "A vibration damper is a device used to minimize the effects of vibration in a structure by dissipating kinetic energy. The damper may be passive (elastic, frictional, inertia) or active (in a system using sensors and actuators)."

msgid "IfcBridge"
msgstr "Bridge"

msgid "IfcBridge_DEFINITION"
msgstr "A Bridge is a civil engineering work that affords passage to pedestrians, animals, vehicles, and services above obstacles or between two points at a height above ground."

msgid "StructureIndicator"
msgstr "Structure Indicator"

msgid "StructureIndicator_DEFINITION"
msgstr "The type of bridge structure (composite, coated, homogeneous or other)."

msgid "StructureIndicator_COATED"
msgstr "Coated"

msgid "StructureIndicator_COMPOSITE"
msgstr "The Type of Bridge Structure (composite"

msgid "StructureIndicator_HOMOGENEOUS"
msgstr "Homogeneous or Other)"

msgid "IfcBridgePart"
msgstr "Bridge Part"

msgid "IfcBridgePart_DEFINITION"
msgstr "Part of a bridge."

msgid "IfcBuilding"
msgstr "Building"

msgid "IfcBuilding_DEFINITION"
msgstr "A building represents a structure that provides shelter for its occupants or contents and stands in one place. The building is also used to provide a basic element within the spatial structure hierarchy for the components of a building project (together with site, storey, and space)."

msgid "BuildingID"
msgstr "Building ID"

msgid "BuildingID_DEFINITION"
msgstr "A unique identifier assigned to a building. A temporary identifier is initially assigned at the time of making a planning application. This temporary identifier is changed to a permanent identifier when the building is registered into a statutory buildings and properties database."

msgid "BuildingID_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "Technical note: in IFC this property takes IfcIdentifier as value."

msgid "ConstructionMethod"
msgstr "Construction Method"

msgid "ConstructionMethod_DEFINITION"
msgstr "The type of construction action to the object, e.g. new construction, renovation, refurbishment, etc."

msgid "ConstructionMethod_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "Technical note: in IFC this property takes IfcLabel as value."

msgid "FireProtectionClass"
msgstr "Fire Protection Class"

msgid "FireProtectionClass_DEFINITION"
msgstr "Main fire protection class for the building which is assigned from the fire protection classification table as given by the relevant national building code."

msgid "FireProtectionClass_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "Technical note: in IFC this property takes IfcLabel as value."

msgid "NumberOfStoreys"
msgstr "Number of Storeys"

msgid "NumberOfStoreys_DEFINITION"
msgstr "The number of storeys within a building.; Captured for those cases where the [[IfcBuildingStorey]] entity is not used. Note that if [[IfcBuildingStorey]] is asserted and the number of storeys in a building can be determined from it, then this approach should be used in preference to setting a property for the number of storeys."

msgid "NumberOfStoreys_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "Technical note: in IFC this property takes IfcCountMeasure as value."

msgid "YearOfConstruction"
msgstr "Year of Construction"

msgid "YearOfConstruction_DEFINITION"
msgstr "Year of construction of this building, including expected year of completion."

msgid "YearOfConstruction_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "Technical note: in IFC this property takes IfcLabel as value."

msgid "YearOfLastRefurbishment"
msgstr "Year of Last Refurbishment"

msgid "YearOfLastRefurbishment_DEFINITION"
msgstr "Year of last major refurbishment, or reconstruction, of the building (applies to reconstruction works)."

msgid "YearOfLastRefurbishment_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "Technical note: in IFC this property takes IfcLabel as value."

msgid "IsLandmarked"
msgstr "Is Landmarked"

msgid "IsLandmarked_DEFINITION"
msgstr "This building is listed as a historic building (TRUE), or not (FALSE), or unknown."

msgid "IsLandmarked_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "Technical note: in IFC this property takes IfcLogical as value."

msgid "ElevationOfRefHeight"
msgstr "Elevation of Ref Height"

msgid "ElevationOfRefHeight_DEFINITION"
msgstr "Elevation above sea level of the reference height used for all storey elevation measures, equals to height 0.0. It is usually the ground floor level."

msgid "ElevationOfRefHeight_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "Technical note: in IFC this property takes IfcLengthMeasure as value."

msgid "ElevationOfTerrain"
msgstr "Elevation of Terrain"

msgid "ElevationOfTerrain_DEFINITION"
msgstr "Elevation above the minimal terrain level around the foot print of the building, given in elevation above sea level."

msgid "ElevationOfTerrain_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "Technical note: in IFC this property takes IfcLengthMeasure as value."

msgid "MarketCategory"
msgstr "Market Category"

msgid "MarketCategory_DEFINITION"
msgstr "[[Category]] of use e.g. residential, commercial, recreation etc."

msgid "MarketCategory_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "Technical note: in IFC this property takes IfcLabel as value."

msgid "MarketSubCategory"
msgstr "Market Sub Category"

msgid "MarketSubCategory_DEFINITION"
msgstr "Subset of category of use e.g. multi-family, 2 bedroom, low rise."

msgid "MarketSubCategory_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "Technical note: in IFC this property takes IfcLabel as value."

msgid "PlanningControlStatus"
msgstr "Planning Control Status"

msgid "PlanningControlStatus_DEFINITION"
msgstr "Label of zoning category or class, or planning control category for the site or facility."

msgid "PlanningControlStatus_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "Technical note: in IFC this property takes IfcLabel as value."

msgid "NarrativeText"
msgstr "Narrative Text"

msgid "NarrativeText_DEFINITION"
msgstr "Added information relating to the adjacent building use that is not appropriate to the general descriptive text associated with an entity through the inherited [[IfcRoot]].[[Description]]."

msgid "VacancyRateInCategoryNow"
msgstr "Vacancy Rate In Category Now"

msgid "VacancyRateInCategoryNow_DEFINITION"
msgstr "Percentage of vacancy found in the particular category currently."

msgid "VacancyRateInCategoryNow_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "Technical note: in IFC this property takes IfcPositiveRatioMeasure as value."

msgid "TenureModesAvailableNow"
msgstr "Tenure Modes Available Now"

msgid "TenureModesAvailableNow_DEFINITION"
msgstr "A list of the tenure modes that are currently available expressed in terms of IfcLabel."

msgid "MarketSubCategoriesAvailableNow"
msgstr "Market Sub Categories Available Now"

msgid "MarketSubCategoriesAvailableNow_DEFINITION"
msgstr "A list of the sub categories of property that are currently available expressed in terms of IfcLabel."

msgid "RentalRatesInCategoryNow"
msgstr "Rental Rates In Category Now"

msgid "RentalRatesInCategoryNow_DEFINITION"
msgstr "Range of the cost rates for property currently available in the required category."

msgid "VacancyRateInCategoryFuture"
msgstr "Vacancy Rate In Category Future"

msgid "VacancyRateInCategoryFuture_DEFINITION"
msgstr "Percentage of vacancy found in the particular category expected in the future."

msgid "VacancyRateInCategoryFuture_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "Technical note: in IFC this property takes IfcPositiveRatioMeasure as value."

msgid "TenureModesAvailableFuture"
msgstr "Tenure Modes Available Future"

msgid "TenureModesAvailableFuture_DEFINITION"
msgstr "A list of the tenure modes that are expected to be available in the future expressed in terms of IfcLabel."

msgid "MarketSubCategoriesAvailableFuture"
msgstr "Market Sub Categories Available Future"

msgid "MarketSubCategoriesAvailableFuture_DEFINITION"
msgstr "A list of the sub categories of property that are expected to be available in the future expressed in terms of IfcLabel."

msgid "RentalRatesInCategoryFuture"
msgstr "Rental Rates In Category Future"

msgid "RentalRatesInCategoryFuture_DEFINITION"
msgstr "Range of the cost rates for property expected to be available in the future in the required category."

msgid "EavesHeight"
msgstr "Eaves Height"

msgid "EavesHeight_DEFINITION"
msgstr "[[Standard]] net height of this storey, from the top surface of the construction floor, to the bottom surface of the construction floor or roof above. Only provided is there is a constant height."

msgid "HeatingWetBulb"
msgstr "Heating Wet Bulb"

msgid "HeatingWetBulb_DEFINITION"
msgstr "Outside wet bulb temperature for heating design."

msgid "HeatingWetBulb_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "Technical note: in IFC this property takes IfcThermodynamicTemperatureMeasure as value."

msgid "HeatingDesignDay"
msgstr "Heating Design Day"

msgid "HeatingDesignDay_DEFINITION"
msgstr "The month, day and time that has been selected for the heating design calculations."

msgid "HeatingDesignDay_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "Technical note: in IFC this property takes IfcDateTime as value."

msgid "CoolingWetBulb"
msgstr "Cooling Wet Bulb"

msgid "CoolingWetBulb_DEFINITION"
msgstr "Outside wet bulb temperature for cooling design."

msgid "CoolingWetBulb_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "Technical note: in IFC this property takes IfcThermodynamicTemperatureMeasure as value."

msgid "CoolingDesignDay"
msgstr "Cooling Design Day"

msgid "CoolingDesignDay_DEFINITION"
msgstr "The month, day and time that has been selected for the cooling design calculations."

msgid "CoolingDesignDay_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "Technical note: in IFC this property takes IfcDateTime as value."

msgid "WeatherDataStation"
msgstr "Weather Data Station"

msgid "WeatherDataStation_DEFINITION"
msgstr "The site weather data station description or reference to the data source from which weather data was obtained for use in calculations."

msgid "WeatherDataDate"
msgstr "Weather Data Date"

msgid "WeatherDataDate_DEFINITION"
msgstr "The date for which the weather data was gathered."

msgid "WeatherDataDate_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "Technical note: in IFC this property takes IfcDateTime as value."

msgid "BuildingThermalExposure"
msgstr "Building Thermal Exposure"

msgid "BuildingThermalExposure_DEFINITION"
msgstr "The thermal exposure expected by the building based on surrounding site conditions."

msgid "BuildingThermalExposure_HEAVY"
msgstr "Heavy"

msgid "BuildingThermalExposure_LIGHT"
msgstr "Light"

msgid "BuildingThermalExposure_MEDIUM"
msgstr "Medium"

msgid "BuildingThermalExposure_NOTKNOWN"
msgstr "Not Known"

msgid "BuildingThermalExposure_UNSET"
msgstr "Unset"

msgid "PrevailingWindDirection"
msgstr "Prevailing Wind Direction"

msgid "PrevailingWindDirection_DEFINITION"
msgstr "The prevailing wind angle direction measured from True North (0 degrees) in a clockwise direction."

msgid "PrevailingWindDirection_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "Technical note: in IFC this property takes IfcPlaneAngleMeasure as value."

msgid "PrevailingWindVelocity"
msgstr "Prevailing Wind Velocity"

msgid "PrevailingWindVelocity_DEFINITION"
msgstr "The design wind velocity coming from the direction specified by the [[PrevailingWindDirection]] attribute."

msgid "PrevailingWindVelocity_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "Technical note: in IFC this property takes IfcLinearVelocityMeasure as value."

msgid "Heat"
msgstr "Heat"

msgid "Heat_DEFINITION"
msgstr "The amount of heat energy consumed during the period specified in the time series."

msgid "Heat_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "Technical note: this is a specific property from IFC that takes as its value a reference to IfcTimeSeries."

msgid "Electricity"
msgstr "Electricity"

msgid "Electricity_DEFINITION"
msgstr "The amount of electricity consumed during the period specified in the time series."

msgid "Electricity_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "Technical note: this is a specific property from IFC that takes as its value a reference to IfcTimeSeries."

msgid "Water"
msgstr "Water"

msgid "Water_DEFINITION"
msgstr "The amount of water consumed during the period specified in the time series."

msgid "Water_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "Technical note: this is a specific property from IFC that takes as its value a reference to IfcTimeSeries."

msgid "Fuel"
msgstr "Fuel"

msgid "Fuel_DEFINITION"
msgstr "The amount of fuel consumed during the period specified in the time series."

msgid "Fuel_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "Technical note: this is a specific property from IFC that takes as its value a reference to IfcTimeSeries."

msgid "Steam"
msgstr "Steam"

msgid "Steam_DEFINITION"
msgstr "The amount of steam consumed during the period specified in the time series."

msgid "Steam_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "Technical note: this is a specific property from IFC that takes as its value a reference to IfcTimeSeries."

msgid "IfcFacilityPartCommon"
msgstr "Facility Part Common"

msgid "IfcFacilityPartCommon_DEFINITION"
msgstr "A part that is not clearly part of one domain but is a hybrid and has shared responsibilities in multiple domains."

msgid "IfcOpeningElement"
msgstr "Opening Element"

msgid "IfcOpeningElement_DEFINITION"
msgstr "The opening element stands for opening, recess or chase, all reflecting voids. It represents a void within any element that has physical manifestation. Openings can be inserted into walls, slabs, beams, columns, or other elements."

msgid "FireRating"
msgstr "Fire Rating"

msgid "FireRating_DEFINITION"
msgstr "Fire rating for this object. It is given according to the national fire safety classification."

msgid "FireRating_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "Technical note: in IFC this property takes IfcLabel as value."

msgid "AcousticRating"
msgstr "Acoustic Rating"

msgid "AcousticRating_DEFINITION"
msgstr "Acoustic rating for this object.; It is provided according to the national building code. It indicates the sound transmission resistance of this object by an index ratio (instead of providing full sound absorption values)."

msgid "AcousticRating_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "Technical note: in IFC this property takes IfcLabel as value."

msgid "Depth"
msgstr "Depth"

msgid "Depth_DEFINITION"
msgstr "The depth of the object."

msgid "IfcProjectionElement"
msgstr "Projection Element"

msgid "IfcProjectionElement_DEFINITION"
msgstr "The projection element is a specialization of the general feature element to represent projections applied to building elements. It represents a solid attached to any element that has physical manifestation."

